    44	/** Each pasted line, in order, puts an OPEN claim on the person it names (compared as names are).
    45	 *  A line whose date and note match claims of that person as they stood before the paste (void and
    46	 *  deleted ones never match) updates the newest DRAFT of them instead: edited to the line's amount
    47	 *  (CLAIM_EDITED when it changes) and opened; a line whose matches include no DRAFT is refused. Any
    48	 *  other line is first checked as {@link net.officefloor.hq.app.claim.AddClaim} checks a claim (its
    49	 *  person on the sheet, not retired before its date, its due-by outside a closed period, its reference
    50	 *  used by no claim on the sheet nor an earlier line), then added (CLAIM_ADDED) and opened. Each claim is
    51	 *  opened as {@link net.officefloor.hq.app.claim.OpenClaim} opens one — numbered in paste order, CLAIM_OPENED then the rollup lines it
    52	 *  moved — and any refusal it would give refuses the whole paste: the transaction is rolled back and the
    53	 *  audit lines, kept until every line went through, are never written. A paste that would take a person
    54	 *  past the sheet's maximum of open claims is refused before anything is written. */
    55	public class PasteClaims {
    56	    private record Pending(Person person, ValidClaim claim, LocalDate date, LocalDate dueBy, String corrects,
    57	            Claim match) {
